# tests/lib/MANIFEST — the CLOSED inventory of shared test EQUIPMENT.
#
# WHY A MANIFEST AND NOT A RULE ABOUT NAMES. The rigs ruling (captain,
# 2026-09-25) has to hold against a path nobody has thought of yet. A gate
# that tries to recognise "this looks like a rig" from a name is a classifier,
# and classifiers in this project have been beaten by rewording every time
# they have been tried. So tests/no-rigs.test.sh does the opposite: it knows
# what is ALLOWED and refuses everything else. This file is the allow-list for
# tests/lib/ — the one place under tests/ that carries executable helpers.
#
# A new file under tests/lib/ FAILS the gate until someone adds a row here.
# That friction is the feature: the inventory can only grow deliberately.
#
# The gate checks three things per row: the file is on disk, it is tracked,
# and its git index mode matches column 1 (so a `git mv` that dropped an
# executable bit is caught). It also checks column 3 against the shipped
# suites, so this file cannot claim a file is exercised when nothing runs it.
#
# COLUMNS:  <git-index-mode> <path> <status> <note>
#   status = exercised  a suite in tests/*.test.sh names it as `lib/<rest>`
#          = unused     deliberately kept, and NO suite names it
#          = doc        documentation; not scanned either way
#
# Paths may not contain spaces.

